; The overheat alarm comes with a reading of 97.5 at activation, and the
; sensor then falls silent: the last value stays in the data, but no reading
; arrives. A value present at activation without an arrival is stale, so the
; temperature is absent at every entry. The controller stops the drive in
; time. The arm moves at 08:00:20; the condition of the prohibition is read in
; the state before the movement, where the temperature is absent, so it is
; undefined: the monitor blocks the movement and the prohibition is not
; breached. Past the 10-minute deadline the invariant is still undefined, not
; false.
(scenario sensor_silent
  (spec "examples/core/sensor_overheat.triel")
  (entry "2026-11-09T08:00:00Z" (activate)
    (data (motor_temp (dec 97.5)) (limit_c (dec 90.0))))
  (entry "2026-11-09T08:00:10Z" (act controller stop_drive must)
    (data (motor_temp (dec 97.5)) (limit_c (dec 90.0))))
  (entry "2026-11-09T08:00:20Z" (act arm move must_not)
    (data (motor_temp (dec 97.5)) (limit_c (dec 90.0))))
  (entry "2026-11-09T08:11:00Z" (tick)
    (data (motor_temp (dec 97.5)) (limit_c (dec 90.0)))))
